{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy","id":1109648,"title":"[2E] Two Spirits - Non-Binary Gender Legacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-30T00:50:18-07:00","id":1109648,"title":"[2E] Two Spirits - Non-Binary Gender Legacy","content":"I want to create fan Legacy for all Non-Binary mage characters, based on Sleepers magcial practices. Around the globe, native cultures often have non-binary persona as rol\u0119 for magical practices or connection with Gods. See this article - <a href=\"http://www.teenvogue.com/story/gender-variance-around-the-world\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.teenvogue.com/story/gende...ound-the-world</a><br /> <br /> Now, we will go into Legacy idea. I only want to mark I'm cis ma\u0142e bisexual bear, so if I make wrong assumptions, point me where. We have official Dakasha Ldgacy, but they connection with Nazis is probkematic to some traditions. <br /> <br /> My idea Legacy is called Two Spirits - name of Legacy is from Native American cultures, but it surely would work around the World. They would be Life/Mind Thyrsus mages, literally becoming other sex person. They would be mostly Nameless, but rise of Free Council and LGBT+ movement remade them in to centralized Libertine Legacy. So what do you think on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T00:54:50-07:00","id":1109650,"title":"","content":"Chrysalides are also non-binary.<br /> <br /> Princes of Masks aren't required to be anything except what they want to be.<br /> <br /> Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T01:09:02-07:00","id":1109653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy#post1109648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do you think on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a painfully wrongheaded and one-note application of a fiction widget revolving around Awakened development in support of a theory of magic or magical theory, particularly given that having a Shadow Name of a different sex or gender is something that happens often enough without characters building an entire magical praxis around that quality alone.<br /> <br /> You have Parent groups, Arcana, and an implicit idea for approximately one Attainment; nothing about this describes a doctrine or symbolset. There's no Legacy here. Get specific. Go more concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T01:14:11-07:00","id":1109655,"title":"","content":"Non-binary gender isn't new for the Awakened. But when talking about Legacies, so far the ones that embrace non-binary gender tend to use it as a tool. The Daksha want to evolve beyond what current humanity is. The Chrysalides pursue their Ideal Form. The Princes of Many Masks are the ultimate Imposters. None of them are pursuing non-binary gender itself as a central Mystery, so if your Legacy is doing exactly that it certainly has a place to fit in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T01:28:27-07:00","id":1109660,"title":"","content":"Echoing Satchel's guidelines, I'd recommend the Legacy have theories and doctrine developed around liminality and liminal beings, with gender a focus to channel their symbols.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T02:27:51-07:00","id":1109669,"title":"","content":"It's still using shape-shifting as a tool. Are non-binary people typically unhappy with being who they are? Trans people I get in those instances where they're stuck in the body of the wrong sex, but I was under the impression that non-binary covers a broader range of folks. <br /> <br /> I feel like Prime's evocation and enforcement of truth might be a viable route, less about changing yourself and more about changing the world to recognize your existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T09:49:19-07:00","id":1110582,"title":"","content":"Hamster, I dunno if you remember the Gay Entitlement thread from way back when or not. Sadly, with the archives gone, I can't refer you directly to it if you haven't.<br /> <br /> If you do remember, then my only advice is to think very hard on how people responded to that before preceding. Because this could very easily fall into the same trap of &quot;organization of [x] being [x] in a tree&quot; all over again.(x then being gay elves, x here being non-binary mages)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T11:31:22-07:00","id":1110604,"title":"","content":"Lumping together every single non-Western gender-divergent identity under one umbrella and giving magical powers based on that smacks of painting with a ludicrously broad brush that erases the unique identity of all involved cultures and is uncomfortable close to &quot;nonwhite/non-binary people are inherently magical!&quot; Speaking of &quot;&quot;&quot;native&quot;&quot;&quot; as some kind of broad shared identity between entirely unrelated peoples and their practices across all continents is the same thing that we all called bullshit back when it was called the Dreamspeakers in the 90s.<br /> <br /> If you wanna make a Legacy of people who use magic to be comfortable in their own skins, go right ahead. If you want to make one that borrows from Sleeper magical traditions practiced by a certain Native American (and it should be specific, not a vague &quot;natives&quot;), sure. But this as presented sounds doomed to offense.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You want a cool trans-inclusive Legacy idea? Make folks who want to rewrite their True Names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 07-02-2017, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T06:56:37-07:00","id":1111240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1110604#post1110604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: You want a cool trans-inclusive Legacy idea? Make folks who want to rewrite their True Names.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be literally everyone. Nine times out of ten Real Name is a boulder on the mage's neck that does nothing but get you killed by a malicious Space specialist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T07:18:50-07:00","id":1111251,"title":"","content":"It's a sympathetic name and not a real or true name for this precise reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T07:44:28-07:00","id":1111260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1110604#post1110604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lumping together every single non-Western gender-divergent identity under one umbrella and giving magical powers based on that smacks of painting with a ludicrously broad brush that erases the unique identity of all involved cultures and is uncomfortable close to &amp;quot;nonwhite/non-binary people are inherently magical!&amp;quot; Speaking of &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;native&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot; as some kind of broad shared identity between entirely unrelated peoples and their practices across all continents is the same thing that we all called bullshit back when it was called the Dreamspeakers in the 90s.<br /> <br /> If you wanna make a Legacy of people who use magic to be comfortable in their own skins, go right ahead. If you want to make one that borrows from Sleeper magical traditions practiced by a certain Native American (and it should be specific, not a vague &amp;quot;natives&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, sure. But this as presented sounds doomed to offense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would the Legacy work as a group that isn't about labeling everyone else with Native American stuff, and instead about trying to spread the idea itself? I do agree on the pitfalls of lumping multiple cultures in a stereotype (as a Korean, I cringed when I heard stuff about Kuei Jin, Hengeyokai and Dreamspeakers)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: You want a cool trans-inclusive Legacy idea? Make folks who want to rewrite their True Names. </div> </div> </div>All mages already left their mark on the Supernal Realm they Awoke to, which became their True identity from that point onwards, Sleeper identity be damned. It's why mages appear as their self-image in the Astral, which can vary in race, gender/sex, and much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T08:06:48-07:00","id":1111270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1111260#post1111260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All mages already left their mark on the Supernal Realm they Awoke to, which became their True identity from that point onwards, Sleeper identity be damned. It's why mages appear as their self-image in the Astral, which can vary in race, gender/sex, and much more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Atamajakki talked about Sympathetic Name, which is the first name any person recognized as their own and there is no official way of actually changing.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of a friend who, due to renaming laws here in Sweden, still has his deadname as a middle name while going by his new first name. Since that law was recently changed he's thinking about getting rid of his deadname completely. I'm guessing it's a bit like that for mages who are trans. They can choose sleeper name and Shadow Name, but they can't rid themselves of their unwanted Sympathetic Name even if nobody knows about it. What's even worse is that their Sympathetic Name might actually be extremely secure due to the whole process. That's got to be infuriating for those who wants nothing to do with their first/assigned identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-04-2017, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T15:32:44-07:00","id":1111426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1111270#post1111270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe Atamajakki talked about Sympathetic Name, which is the first name any person recognized as their own and there is no official way of actually changing.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of a friend who, due to renaming laws here in Sweden, still has his deadname as a middle name while going by his new first name. Since that law was recently changed he's thinking about getting rid of his deadname completely. I'm guessing it's a bit like that for mages who are trans. They can choose sleeper name and Shadow Name, but they can't rid themselves of their unwanted Sympathetic Name even if nobody knows about it. What's even worse is that their Sympathetic Name might actually be extremely secure due to the whole process. That's got to be infuriating for those who wants nothing to do with their first/assigned identity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I see. Then it becomes less about gender, and more about transcending past identities in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T19:15:52-07:00","id":1111500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1111270#post1111270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe Atamajakki talked about Sympathetic Name, which is the first name any person recognized as their own and there is no official way of actually changing.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of a friend who, due to renaming laws here in Sweden, still has his deadname as a middle name while going by his new first name. Since that law was recently changed he's thinking about getting rid of his deadname completely. I'm guessing it's a bit like that for mages who are trans. They can choose sleeper name and Shadow Name, but they can't rid themselves of their unwanted Sympathetic Name even if nobody knows about it. What's even worse is that their Sympathetic Name might actually be extremely secure due to the whole process. That's got to be infuriating for those who wants nothing to do with their first/assigned identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's frustrated me for quite some time that a game where you rage against an oppressive Gnostic machine offers literally no canon way (short of Ascension) to transcend a label thrust upon you by others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T10:32:24-07:00","id":1111707,"title":"","content":"Isn't there an Imperial spell or something that can change your Sympathetic Name? I thought in 2e that is the current use of the term &quot;True Name&quot;, that's the spell and/or term for after the spell is used.<br /> <br /> I think Dave said that here on the forums somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T10:55:51-07:00","id":1111716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1111707#post1111707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there an Imperial spell or something that can change your Sympathetic Name? I thought in 2e that is the current use of the term &quot;True Name&quot;, that's the spell and/or term for after the spell is used.<br /> <br /> I think Dave said that here on the forums somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't change it, instead it severs your Sympathetic connection to it for the spell's Duration. In other words you don't get to have a Sympathetic Name for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:20:21-07:00","id":1111773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1111716#post1111716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't change it, instead it severs your Sympathetic connection to it for the spell's Duration. In other words you don't get to have a Sympathetic Name for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial Magic spell to erase your Sympathetic Name is permanent, like most of Archmasters magic.<br /> <br /> But it's still is not solution to Topic Idea as... Archmasters are rare. I look here to make Legacy for entering on non-binary magic from mage character creation ( with Gnosis 2 ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:48:46-07:00","id":1111784,"title":"","content":"I was mostly responding to Lex and the others talking about wanting to change your Sympathetic Name.<br /> <br /> I agree with the others that say that the specific idea in the OP is not very well done. A more generic legacy about not being who you feel you should be seems better. Not specifically non-binary and not tied to an awkward 'Native American' culture. Pick a specific culture to tie it to or not tie it to any culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T00:49:47-07:00","id":1112002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1111784#post1111784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the others that say that the specific idea in the OP is not very well done. A more generic legacy about not being who you feel you should be seems better. Not specifically non-binary and not tied to an awkward 'Native American' culture. Pick a specific culture to tie it to or not tie it to any culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would went with not tieing to specific culture, as we would have like 30 various Legacy, on more or less the same idea. Name was only 'placeholder' for anything, so if have something more general, I'm all ears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T08:34:42-07:00","id":1112122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1112002#post1112002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would went with not tieing to specific culture, as we would have like 30 various Legacy, on more or less the same idea. Name was only 'placeholder' for anything, so if have something more general, I'm all ears.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The name would depend on the specific idea behind the legacy. If you go with Lex's idea about a Legacy focused on changing their Sympathetic Name and have a philosophy and Attainments based on that then you could go with something like 'Aletheian Onym' (based on the Greek for 'True Name').<br /> <br /> If you want to preserve more of your original idea though, then you will need to work out the details of it and come up with a name based on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T08:46:55-07:00","id":1112128,"title":"","content":"In real life, two-spirit orientation is a distinct identity within its own cultural framework. It's not really just another name for being non-binary, because non-binary identity is based on gender and sexuality models outside of that framework. In Canada, we now customarily include it alongside other identities, such as in the LGBTQ2 term.<br /> <br /> So this Legacy is a mistake. It's kind of like creating a Legacy called &quot;Lesbian.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:04:47-07:00","id":1112871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1111500#post1111500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's frustrated me for quite some time that a game where you rage against an oppressive Gnostic machine offers literally no canon way (short of Ascension) to transcend a label thrust upon you by others.</div> </div> </div> </div>There kinda isn't a good solution to this.<br /> If the Sympathetic Name can be changed no strings attached, then it's meaningless as a gameplay mechanic and we can just scrap the whole thing. I generate a 256 symbols long alphanumeric string, declare it my name, burn down the computer and blast myself with vodka and Mind spells until I'm sure that the name will never be recovered. Now I'm personally not against scrapping the name mechanic, but I'm sure some people will be.<br /> If the Sympathetic Name is aquired through association and sympathy, then Shadow Names don't work. Many (possibly even most) mages would consider their magical identity to be their main identity and the mundane persona to be something to grow out of. Which means your Shadow Name will become your Sympathetic Name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T22:23:35-07:00","id":1113597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1111500#post1111500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's frustrated me for quite some time that a game where you rage against an oppressive Gnostic machine offers literally no canon way (short of Ascension) to transcend a label thrust upon you by others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds easier in Demon than Mage, honestly. Probably has to do with how the whole &quot;Atlantean&quot; conflict against the Exarchs has been downplayed in 2E, in favor of &quot;explore the Mysteries of the World&quot; angle.<br /> <br /> Hmm... a chronicle where you overthrow (or at least heavily damage) The Father would be partly a game about transcending gender labels. I'd play that, if only to get a sense of this whole gender issue (which I'm largely oblivious at, being cisgender &amp; heterosexual)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T05:56:05-07:00","id":1113695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1113597#post1113597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds easier in Demon than Mage, honestly. Probably has to do with how the whole &quot;Atlantean&quot; conflict against the Exarchs has been downplayed in 2E, in favor of &quot;explore the Mysteries of the World&quot; angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Atlantean stuff is downplayed, but 2e is a lot more explicit about the Exarchs and the gnostic elements of the setting. The Awakened obsess about mysteries precisely because it allows them to grasp the Supernal again.<br /> <br /> In that context I tend to think sympathetic names being really hard to get round is kinda the point. It's not just any label, it's the first label the world gives you. Awakening doesn't let you transcend the Lie, it merely makes you aware of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T20:32:37-07:00","id":1114015,"title":"","content":"If you do feel resentful of a Sympathetic Name or a gender identifier, there is a quick and easy way to be rid of it. Bathe in the Ocean Oroboros. Quick and easy in this case meaning that you don't have to hunt down an archmaster or render your soul into an immutable shape in order to complete the objective.<br /> <br /> You could also build a Death-centric legacy focused on finding the Ocean of Fragments in the Underworld and ridding yourself of identifiers you don't want, finding ones you do want, and incorporating those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-09-2017, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T20:23:27-07:00","id":1114380,"title":"","content":"You could also use Time magic to rewrite your past to get a new name, for that matter. In 2E, that would be permanent.<br /> Space should also be able to do this by Mastery, at least. (Maybe with a little Prime or Mind)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T20:32:38-07:00","id":1114382,"title":"","content":"An Abyssal could likely do it, too. They seem to be the only thing outside of the Gnostic machine, anyhow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-10-2017, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T20:48:42-07:00","id":1114391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114382#post1114382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Abyssal could likely do it, too. They seem to be the only thing outside of the Gnostic machine, anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would rather not go with Abyssal route on this - it would be... very mixed massage for non-binary players...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T21:14:00-07:00","id":1114401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1112128#post1112128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In real life, two-spirit orientation is a distinct identity within its own cultural framework. It's not really just another name for being non-binary, because non-binary identity is based on gender and sexuality models outside of that framework. In Canada, we now customarily include it alongside other identities, such as in the LGBTQ2 term.<br /> <br /> So this Legacy is a mistake. It's kind of like creating a Legacy called &quot;Lesbian.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Two spirit is its own separate identity within a spectrum of non-bianary id\u00e9nties. As for ending up with 30 differnet identical legacies... you wouldn't. That's kinda the point we're making. Not all cultures would develop the Legacy in the first place. Even if they did, a non-bianary Niisitapi Legacy would be very different from a non-bianary Nakoda and a non-bianary Tsu Tina Legacy, and four nations live within a couple hours drive of each other. By saying that you're saving yourself work, what you are actually doing is erasing all of those people and putting a stereotype in their place. <br /> <br /> Remember when you expressed your frustration in the Dark Eras 2 thread because you had to correct someone on peaceful vs violent resistance to the USSR (I think?) in Poland, because they proposed an era based off of a massive misconception of your history? This legacy as it stands would be doing the exact same thing to someone else's history and culture. And it's repeating the same cultural erasure that has been the policy of the Canadian and American governments until recently as a form of cultural and biological genocide and apartheid. It is a no go zone.<br /> <br /> And I swear I'm not trying to be harsh. Just realistic and straight to the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T21:17:50-07:00","id":1114405,"title":"","content":"IMO, after you find a way to strip yourself of gender identifiers or Sympathy that you don't want you haven't done shit to further the cause to anyone else.<br /> <br /> A legacy, or a trip to the Ocean Oroboros, or to the Ocean of Fragments might have you feeling better about yourself. It does nothing for those that come after you though. Legacies can technically affect more than yourself, but it will always be a smaller subsection of the non-binary folks than you and your close allies compromise.<br /> <br /> If it's just all about you then Legacy away, but don't pretend that it helps your unAwakened comrades still being suffocated by the way the world currently is.<br /> <br /> I kind of feel that people look at Legacies as a way to fix things. Really though, that's just retreating into denial. There is shit to do that just being in a Legacy can't fix, and being in a Legacy lets you feel like you've broken free of the Lie, while in reality you're just enslaving yourself to a new Lie. That is, I think, the greatest problem that social justice Legacies face.<br /> <br /> You can't just break the boundaries for yourself. A true non- binary legacy would seek to break the entire gender system itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T21:56:28-07:00","id":1114423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114391#post1114391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would rather not go with Abyssal route on this - it would be... very mixed massage for non-binary players...</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant for changing names, but one shouldn't think so poorly about the Abyss, especially when the Fallen World is a prison controlled by the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T22:12:53-07:00","id":1114435,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> : Perfectly said.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> : Why would it be a social justice Legacy? A Legacy is a unique opportunity to reshape yourself on a metaphysical level. I would assume the vast majority of transgender Legacies would be developed as a type of transitioning rather than wasting such a golden opportunity to just gain additional tools for activism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T23:37:59-07:00","id":1114458,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> - I admit, I do not know enough about other cultures to write more than maybe 3-4 examples of their counterpart non-binary Legacies. But if Dreamspeakers Legacy are a thing in Mage for native 'animalistic avatars embracers in Astral', similar can be made for the non-binary, identity seeking younger mages. It will be much more Free Council counterculture thing than original beliefs, but it still work in the setting. I think Dreamspeakers also gone this evolution - from original beliefs native Legacy that begun to die out and then, in start of globalization ( i.e. colonialism era ) becoming more and more as one universal Legacies from scratch. Something like Tremere Nameless Order from all those previous Reapers Legacies thing ( without soul predation, of course ).<br /> <br /> If someone want to make particular Legacies for each native culture, you can easily make one and I encourage it even - would likely read this.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114435#post1114435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Legacy is a unique opportunity to reshape yourself on a metaphysical level. I would assume the vast majority of transgender Legacies would be developed as a type of transitioning rather than wasting such a golden opportunity to just gain additional tools for activism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is place for both groups in setting - native Legacies as slowly disappearing more limited traditions. And new Free Council 'non-binary punkers', wanting to be free of Exarchs on tide of LGBT+ activism from start of 70s.<br /> <br /> And I start to think that those 'we want to cast away our Sympathy Names rebels' Legacy will be Space based - on 5th Attainment they could get this True Name archmastery-like effect, as pinnacle of Legacy. ( Using one Archmastery personal effect sounds as thing fitting to the whole unique Legacy Attainments thing. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-11-2017, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T04:45:44-07:00","id":1114525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114423#post1114423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just meant for changing names, but one shouldn't think so poorly about the Abyss, especially when the Fallen World is a prison controlled by the Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all for positive definitions for the Abyss. Garden of Eden would be in the Abyss, as Primal Wilds are very clearly a darwinistic dog eats dog hellhole. Heaven would be in the Abyss because Underworld is distinctly not that. The world of universal peace and acceptance would be in the Abyss because Pandemonium is defined by infinitely harassing you until your skin is thick enough to not give a shit. Etc., etc. But alas, mage writers seem to focus on leper-outcast-unclean aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Left-Handed Path</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Deluge (Obrimos):</b><br /> Instead of climbing to celestial light, Joined Obrimos drown in blood-tainted floodwaters. Aquatic demons harass them. Endless chains converge on a sea floor littered with devastated temples. They wrap around the <i>Iriyim</i>: watcher-angels who taught humanity forbidden knowledge. Obrimos invoke their powers and summon the attributes of the fallen ones\u2019 Nephilim children.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You see, evil Obrimos hear angels like normal Obrimos... but they are <b><i>EVIL</i></b> angels! Bad angels! Oogly-boogly-boo!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Acanthus one is especially pathetic.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ao Si, the Mound of Thorns (Acanthus):</b><br /> Joined Acanthus call upon the twisted Fomorians and Norse rot-elves they found in the ever-shifting, thorny maze of their Dur-Abzu. Their rites recall legendary broken oaths, kin-slaying heroes and inescapable curses. </div> </div> </div>Like, is that somehow different from normal Arcadia? Because it sounds like the goth night in Arcadia and all the elves are wearing eyeliner. So they are <i>rot</i>-elves!<br /> <br /> For the realm of impossible unreality Abyss seems to be really stuck with generic black evil tentacle imagery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T04:58:07-07:00","id":1114528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114525#post1114525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for positive definitions for the Abyss. Garden of Eden would be in the Abyss, as Primal Wilds are very clearly a darwinistic dog eats dog hellhole. Heaven would be in the Abyss because Underworld is distinctly not that. The world of universal peace and acceptance would be in the Abyss because Pandemonium is defined by infinitely harassing you until your skin is thick enough to not give a shit. Etc., etc. But alas, mage writers seem to focus on leper-outcast-unclean aspect.<br /> <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;You see, evil Obrimos hear angels like normal Obrimos... but they are <b><i>EVIL</i></b> angels! Bad angels! Oogly-boogly-boo!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The Acanthus one is especially pathetic.<br /> <br /> Like, is that somehow different from normal Arcadia? Because it sounds like the goth night in Arcadia and all the elves are wearing eyeliner. So they are <i>rot</i>-elves!<br /> <br /> For the realm of impossible unreality Abyss seems to be really stuck with generic black evil tentacle imagery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blame its marketing department? I suppose Abyssal PR might focus more on negative impressions and driving people away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T05:02:22-07:00","id":1114529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114528#post1114528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blame its marketing department? I suppose Abyssal PR might focus more on negative impressions and driving people away.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real marketing departments already do that, so can't be Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Which is sort of the main problem with the Abyss. If you define the antagonist as &quot;unreality&quot; - what the heck is it? Anything we might imagine is by definition part of reality, and Abyss is supposed to be not that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T05:03:32-07:00","id":1114530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114528#post1114528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blame its marketing department? I suppose Abyssal PR might focus more on negative impressions and driving people away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971430#post971430\">culture warfare purposes</a>. I think the Neolithic age really helped point that out, but also second edition isn't meshing out of character stuff with in character perspective so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-11-2017, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T08:34:56-07:00","id":1114602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114525#post1114525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for positive definitions for the Abyss. Garden of Eden would be in the Abyss, as Primal Wilds are very clearly a darwinistic dog eats dog hellhole. Heaven would be in the Abyss because Underworld is distinctly not that. The world of universal peace and acceptance would be in the Abyss because Pandemonium is defined by infinitely harassing you until your skin is thick enough to not give a shit. Etc., etc. But alas, mage writers seem to focus on leper-outcast-unclean aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The underworld was not meant to be Heaven in the first place. Its supposed to be Purgatory. I'm guessing, given the context, that you actually mean Stygia, instead of the Underworld, which is a different &quot;place.&quot; Well, same purpose - never meant to be heaven, but purgatory.<br /> <br /> Thanks to Dark Eras, we know the 2e Watchtowers shift in appearance and symbolism depending on time and culture. The Thyrsus tower is not linked to the idea of a christian Garden of Eden. We have dank tunels, rainstorms, wild seas, and more. While Eden may have been an initial idea, the game very quickly deviated from that early on. Garden of Eden is much more likely to be another Time Before civilization in 2e paradigm than anything else. <br /> <br /> You can do what you like in your games, but I don't think the associations you're making here are really the intent at all. I'm still not sure why universal peace is supposed to come the Abode of Demons in the first place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T08:44:17-07:00","id":1114606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114602#post1114602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thyrsus tower is not linked to the idea of a christian Garden of Eden.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... huh? I said that the Primal Wild is <i><b><u>not</u></b></i> a Garden of Eden. That it's a place that is very opposite to the Garden of Eden. You are not going to see a tiger and a lamb drinking together in the Primal Wild because that's not how the Primal Wild works. Which means the Garden of Eden, the opposite of the Primal Wild where everything peacefully coexists (and possibly bows down before Man), must be in the Abyss. To quote from the wiki:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Wild</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">These denizens of the jungle all want their toll in blood, even the trees and vines, for blood is the currency of the Primal Wild\u2019s jungles; all have their own means of obtaining it. All creatures are enhanced beyond the limits of their Fallen World counterparts; predators are stronger and deadlier, prey are faster and more numerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T09:32:16-07:00","id":1114640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114606#post1114606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... huh? I said that the Primal Wild is <i><b><u>not</u></b></i> a Garden of Eden. That it's a place that is very opposite to the Garden of Eden. You are not going to see a tiger and a lamb drinking together in the Primal Wild because that's not how the Primal Wild works. Which means the Garden of Eden, the opposite of the Primal Wild where everything peacefully coexists (and possibly bows down before Man), must be in the Abyss. To quote from the wiki:</div> </div> </div> </div> That's still illogical. The Abyss is not supposed to be a direct opposite, and just because something doesn't exist in the Thyrsus Truths doesn't mean another Path's Truths can't embody it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T10:11:03-07:00","id":1114657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114525#post1114525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for positive definitions for the Abyss. Garden of Eden would be in the Abyss, as Primal Wilds are very clearly a darwinistic dog eats dog hellhole. Heaven would be in the Abyss because Underworld is distinctly not that. The world of universal peace and acceptance would be in the Abyss because Pandemonium is defined by infinitely harassing you until your skin is thick enough to not give a shit. Etc., etc. But alas, mage writers seem to focus on leper-outcast-unclean aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's literally what the sample Aswadim in Left-Hand Path wants to do. Good example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, is that somehow different from normal Arcadia? </div> </div> </div>If you read paragraph just before those descriptions you'd know what was going on:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dur-Abzu collect the contradictions and taboos of Path mythology instead, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T10:12:46-07:00","id":1114659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114525#post1114525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You see, evil Obrimos hear angels like normal Obrimos... but they are <b><i>EVIL</i></b> angels! Bad angels! Oogly-boogly-boo!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The reflection of the domain of forces of power and form that hold to standards of behavior that may be near-impossible for humans to maintain constantly is a broken-down flooded wreck inhabited by the offspring of those forces' transgressions. Because that's the kind of narrative the undoing of a symbolic cornerstone of reality with those qualities draws on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Acanthus one is especially pathetic.<br /> <br /> Like, is that somehow different from normal Arcadia? Because it sounds like the goth night in Arcadia and all the elves are wearing eyeliner. So they are <i>rot</i>-elves! </div> </div> </div>The reflection of the place where reality runs on things being temporary and words being kept is not maintained by kinslayers and oathbreakers and the stultifying entrapment of arbitrary inescapable punishment. Arcadia's undoing is built on the tale of fae beings associated with the breakdown of agreements and the unconditional curtailing of choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the realm of impossible unreality Abyss seems to be really stuck with generic black evil tentacle imagery. </div> </div> </div>The Abyss is not its Watchtower-equivalents, but its Watchtower-equivalents are built to negate the symbolism of their Supernal counterparts. &quot;Impossible unreality&quot; still has to manifest in ways you can perceive in order to be a usable fiction widget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T10:51:41-07:00","id":1114668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109648-2e-two-spirits-non-binary-gender-legacy?p=1114606#post1114606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... huh? I said that the Primal Wild is <i><b><u>not</u></b></i> a Garden of Eden. That it's a place that is very opposite to the Garden of Eden. You are not going to see a tiger and a lamb drinking together in the Primal Wild because that's not how the Primal Wild works. Which means the Garden of Eden, the opposite of the Primal Wild where everything peacefully coexists (and possibly bows down before Man), must be in the Abyss. To quote from the wiki:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While the Garden of Eden might exist in the Abyss, that still isn't what the matching Ziggurat would be. It's a subversion of the Path's Watchtower, not an exact opposite. The Abyssal Garden of Eden that actually embodies those ideals isn't mentioned because there is no plot there. Perfectly happy and reasonable bits of Abyss don't try to encroach on reality and do terrible things that cause mages to get involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}